{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.048,
            0.419,
            0.065
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.091,
            0.599,
            0.115
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "1.2 Percentage of Some Quantity"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.122,
            0.601,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": "? **Example 1:** Madhu and Madhav each ate biscuits of a different variety. Madhu’s biscuits had 25% sugar, while Madhav’s had 35% sugar. Can you tell who ate more sugar?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.198,
            0.602,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": "As we just saw, percentages represent fractional quantities or proportions. It would be inappropriate to compare just the percentages when they are referring to different quantities or wholes. That is, if they"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.616,
            0.125,
            0.872,
            0.279
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.288,
            0.848,
            0.346
          ],
          "continues_prev": true,
          "content": "both had 100 g of biscuits, then clearly Madhav ate more sugar — 35 g (35% of 100 g is 35 g per 100 g) vs. Madhu’s 25 g (25% of 100 g is 25 g per 100 g)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.351,
            0.844,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": "? Suppose Madhu ate 120 g of biscuits and Madhav ate 95 g of biscuits. Who consumed more sugar? Try to find out."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.395,
            0.847,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": "We know that the weight of sugar is proportional to the weight of the biscuits consumed. Madhu ate 120 g of biscuits having 25% sugar. The amount of sugar he ate is the value in the blank —"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.401,
            0.454,
            0.596,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": "25:100 \\cdots :120.",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.479,
            0.547,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": "A few ways of going forward are shown."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.512,
            0.549,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": "| 25% sugar means - 25 g sugar per 100 g of biscuits, which means 5 g sugar per 20 g | The proportional relationship can be written as ${ \\frac { 2 5 } { 1 0 0 } } = { \\frac { s } { 1 2 0 } } .$ |\n| --- | --- |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_table_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.579,
            0.513,
            0.864,
            0.632
          ],
          "content": "| 0 | 25% | 50% | 75% | 100% |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | I |  | I |  |\n|  | I |  | I |  |\n|  | Sugar | I |  |  |\n|  |  | 1 |  |  |\n|  | I | - - | - - |  |\n| 0 | 30 g | 60 g | 90 g | 120 g |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_table_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.665,
            0.845,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": "Do any of the methods match your thinking? Were you able to understand all the methods?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.702,
            0.848,
            0.757
          ],
          "content": "Now, let us find out how much sugar Madhav ate. He ate 95 g of biscuits with 35% sugar. Sometimes the numbers may not be convenient to calculate using different methods as we did just before."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.757,
            0.581,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": "100 g of the biscuits he ate has 35 g of sugar."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.779,
            0.646,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": "This means, 1 g of the biscuits has $\\frac { 3 5 } { 1 0 0 }$ g of sugar."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.731,
            0.759,
            0.88,
            0.789
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{35}{100} = \\frac{x}{1} \\rightarrow x = \\frac{35}{100}",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.805,
            0.79,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": "We can say that 95 g of the biscuit will have $\\frac{35}{100} \\;  g  \\times 95 = 33.25 \\;  g .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.831,
            0.845,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": "This can also be solved by finding the value of s in the proportional relationship $\\frac { 3 5 } { 1 0 0 } = \\frac { s } { 9 5 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.881,
            0.526,
            0.9
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, Madhav ate more sugar."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.093,
            0.915,
            0.114,
            0.934
          ],
          "content": "6"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
